le2 currently relies on the backend to correctly limit file paths to `SENDFILE_ROOT`. This is not the case for the `simple` and `development` backends, it is also not necessarily the case for any of the other backends either (it's just an assumption that was made by the original author).\n\nThis will be fixed in 0.6.0 which is to be released the same day as this advisory is made public.\n\nWhen upgrading, you will need to make sure `SENDFILE_ROOT` is set in your settings module if it wasn't already.","fixed_in":["0.6.0"],"id":"GHSA-6r3c-8xf3-ggrr","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-6r3c-8xf3-ggrr","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null},{"aliases":[],"details":"Similar to CVE-2022-36359 for Django, django-sendfile2 did not protect against a reflected file download attack in version 0.6.1 and earlier. If the file name used by django-sendfile2 was derived from user input, then it would be possible to perform a such an attack. A new version of django-sendfile2 will be released. Either download django-sendfile2 0.7.0 as a workaround or sanitize user input yourself, using Django's patch as a template: https://github.com/django/django/commit/bd062445cffd3f6cc6dcd20d13e2abed818fa173","fixed_in":["0.7.0"],"id":"GHSA-pcjh-6r5h-r92r","link":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-pcjh-6r5h-r92r","source":"osv","summary":null,"withdrawn":null}]},"0.4.1":{"info":{"author":"Matt Molyneaux","author_email":"moggers87+git@moggers87.co.uk","bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":["Development Status :: 4 - Beta","Environment :: Web Environment","Framework :: Django","Intended Audience :: Developers","License :: OSI Approved :: BSD License","Operating System :: OS Independent","Programming Language :: Python","Programming Language :: Python :: 2","Programming Language :: Python :: 2.7","Programming Language :: Python :: 3","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.3","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.4","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.5","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.